; A C directive must not close a cycle of conversions (issue #1065), but
; that check compared the exact commodities written, from a link past
; each.  So it missed a commodity converted into itself, directly, through
; an alias or from an annotated form, which failed an assertion or linked
; the commodity to itself, and a cycle closed through annotated forms,
; which ran amounts round the chain into numbers like 2^100 (found while
; fixing issue #3261).

commodity USD
    alias $

C 1 $ = 1 $
C 1 $ = 2 $
C 1 USD = 1 $
C 1 X {$1} = 1 X
C 1 X = 1 X {$1}
C 1 A = 2 B
C 1 B {$1} = 3 A {$2}

test bal -> 6
__ERROR__
While parsing file "$FILE", line 12:
Error: Commodity conversion would create a cycle
While parsing file "$FILE", line 13:
Error: Commodity conversion would create a cycle
While parsing file "$FILE", line 14:
Error: Commodity conversion would create a cycle
While parsing file "$FILE", line 15:
Error: Commodity conversion would create a cycle
While parsing file "$FILE", line 16:
Error: Commodity conversion would create a cycle
While parsing file "$FILE", line 18:
Error: Commodity conversion would create a cycle
end test
